The legal texts come from official publications of the Republic of Senegal:

  Journal officiel de la République du Sénégal, n° 6406 du 3 mai 2008, Loi n° 2008-12 du 25 janvier 2008 portant
  sur la Protection des données à caractère personnel, web edition http://www.jo.gouv.sn/spip.php?article6663,
  read from the Internet Archive capture of 9 June 2015
  (https://web.archive.org/web/20150609214903/http://www.jo.gouv.sn/spip.php?article6663), retrieved 28 October 2026;
  Conseil constitutionnel du Sénégal, Loi organique n° 2016-23 du 14 juillet 2016 relative au Conseil
  constitutionnel (JORS NS 6946 du 15 juillet 2016, pp. 927-930), https://conseilconstitutionnel.sn/la-loi-organique/,
  retrieved 28 October 2026.

The Journal officiel site read "© Copyrights Gouvernement du Sénégal" and the Conseil constitutionnel's site reads
"© Copyright 2026. tous droits réservés"; neither publishes a licence for the legal texts. They are official legal
texts; their copyright status is not confirmed here, and they are reproduced with the attribution above. Two words
of Loi n° 2008-12 were corrected from the copy published by the Commission de Protection des Données Personnelles
(https://www.cdp.sn/sites/default/files/protection.pdf, Internet Archive capture of 1 March 2017), as listed in
REPRODUCE.md.

Changes made by Lexifina: the text was converted to one Markdown file per provision, one paragraph per line;
spacing, apostrophes, quotes and dashes were normalised; headings, the exposé des motifs, the enacting and executory
formulas and the signatures were removed; and the text was arranged as git commits credited to the laws concerned.
The wording of the law was not otherwise changed. None of the publishers endorses this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the tools) are
dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
